{"id": "unknown-2026-06-11-040", "date": "2026-06-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Residential PV costs fell 7% year over year in Brazil", "content": "<p>Residential solar PV costs in Brazil fell 7% year on year to BRL 2.45/W, driven by lower equipment prices amid global oversupply, with several states offering below-average installation costs.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/11/el-precio-medio-de-la-energia-solar-en-brasil-retrocede-un-7-en-un-ano/\">Residential PV costs fell 7% year over year in Brazil</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/11/el-precio-medio-de-la-energia-solar-en-brasil-retrocede-un-7-en-un-ano/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-11-041", "date": "2026-06-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Tongwei debuts BIFIMAX module for projects requiring high-bifaciality", "content": "<p>With 90±5% bifaciality, TNC BIFIMAX 670 W can reduce CAPEX by 0.87 euro cents per Watt. The new solution, designed for high-latitude, high-albedo markets, will be showcased by Tongwei at this year’s Intersolar Europe in Munich. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/11/tongwei-debuts-bifimax-module-for-projects-requiring-high-bifaciality/\">Tongwei debuts BIFIMAX module for projects requiring high-bifaciality</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/11/tongwei-debuts-bifimax-module-for-projects-requiring-high-bifaciality/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-11-042", "date": "2026-06-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cathode_material", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["loss", "decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "One-year outdoor testing reveals degradation paths in perovskite tandem solar cells", "content": "<p>Researchers from TNO and Fraunhofer ISE ran a 1-year outdoor test of perovskite/perovskite/silicon triple-junction solar cells and found a clear efficiency decline from 17–18% to 13–14% driven by multi-stage degradation. The main failure mechanisms were voltage loss, encapsulation delamination, and UV/thermal-induced interface and transport-layer degradation rather than intrinsic absorber instability.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/11/one-year-outdoor-testing-rev", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/11/one-year-outdoor-testing-reveals-degradation-paths-in-perovskite-tandem-solar-cells/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-11-043", "date": "2026-06-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase", "improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Solar module cooling tech based on perforated fins", "content": "<p>Researchers in Algeria simulated perforated hexagonal-fin heat sinks to improve PV cooling performance using CFD analysis. The best design reduced cell temperature by up to 20.93% and increased efficiency while maintaining high thermal performance under forced convection.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/11/solar-module-cooling-tech-based-on-perforated-fins/\">Solar module cooling tech based on perforated fins</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.c", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/11/solar-module-cooling-tech-based-on-perforated-fins/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-11-044", "date": "2026-06-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["outperform", "improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Study finds tandem PV has 30% lower environmental impact than crystalline silicon", "content": "<p>A Spanish research team conducted a cradle-to-gate LCA of eight PV technologies across three generations, finding that tandem solar cells can outperform silicon-based systems in environmental terms due to higher efficiencies. However, cadmium telluride thin-film technologies still show the lowest overall impacts, while tandem systems require long lifetimes and improved stability to deliver clear sustainability advantages over established PV technologies.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.p", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/11/study-finds-tandem-pv-has-30-lower-environmental-impact-than-crystalline-silicon/", "type": "rss"}]}
